From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: The desktop's icons at 32, 48 or 64 pixels, at the system's scale.

The desktop showed the system's large icons, 32 pixels at 100 %, and
nothing changed it. As in Windows 10, its View menu has Large, Medium and
Small icons (64, 48 and 32 pixels at 100 %, Medium the default), kept in
HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\Shell\Bags\1\Desktop\IconSize and
multiplied by the system's scale. The icon cache keeps a third list for the
desktop, index for index the same icons as the small and large ones, taken
from the files at the desktop's size (the large icon scaled when a file has
none of it). Another size, from the menu or from the Display panel
(WM_SETTINGCHANGE "DesktopIconSize"), takes every cached icon again at the
new size and lays the desktop out in the new grid. Other folders keep the
system's large icons.
